tion, beats everything.\n        13. Quadplex set: a quad with two single cards OR two pairs attached.\n        Use the EXACT card symbols provided in the Valid Moves list.\n        Prepare a valid JSON object like {"cards": ["♠3", "♥3"]} for your answer, along with your explanation and reason. If you pass, output: {"cards": []}\n        \n        Now is your turn, to your best ability, choose your move to maximize your chances of winning.\n        Please briefly evaluate a few proimsing moves, provide reason for your final choice, and output the action with specified format.\n        Your response format should be:\n        Evaluation: [Your Evaluation]\n        Reason: [Your Reason]\n        Answer: [Your Answer]\n    ', 'user_prompt': "You are playing as a peasant. Your aim is to be the play out all your cards before the landlord does, OR help your teammate (the other peasant) play out their cards before the landlord does. If the landlord plays out all cards first, you lose.\nYou are a Peasant. The Previous Player (Left) is the Landlord (ENEMY). The Next Player (Right) is your TEAMMATE (Peasant). You must cooperate with your teammate to beat the Landlord. The objective is to empty your hand before the landlord does, or help your teammate empty their hand before the landlord does.\n\nYour Hand: ♣7\nLast Play to Beat: None (Free Play)\n--- Game History (Recent) ---\nTurn 4 (You): ♥3 ♦3\nTurn 5 (Next Player): Pass\nTurn 5 (Prev Player): ♠5 ♦5\nTurn 5 (You): Pass\nTurn 6 (Next Player): ♥8 ♦8\nTurn 6 (Prev Player): Pass\nTurn 6 (You): Pass\nTurn 7 (Next Player): ♠3\nTurn 7 (Prev Player): ♦7\nTurn 7 (You): ♣K\nTurn 8 (Next Player): Pass\nTurn 8 (Prev Player): ♦A\nTurn 8 (You): ♠6 ♥6 ♣6 ♦6\nTurn 9 (Next Player): Pass\nTurn 9 (Prev Player): Pass\n--- Player Info ---\nCards Held by Next Player (Right) [Peasant (Teammate)]: 14\nCards Held by Prev Player (Left) [Landlord (Opponent)]: 4\n--- Cards Remaining Unknown (Card Counting) ---\n(Format explanation: 'Rank: Count', e.g., '2: 4' means there are four 2s left unknown)\nRedJoker: 1, BlackJoker: 1, 2: 1, A: 2, K: 1, Q: 2, J: 2, 10: 2, 9: 2, 8: 1, 7: 1, 5: 1, 4: 1\nValid Moves:\nsingle: ♣7\n\nSelect the best move from the Valid Moves list above. You can choose to pass even if you have valid moves that can beat the previous play, but you cannot pass if you are in a Free Play (no last play).\nEnsure your response matches one of the valid moves exactly.\nRemember to provide Explanation, Reason, and Answer.", 'reasoning': "**A Simple Win**\n\nAlright, here's the situation. I'm a peasant in this game of Fight the Landlord, and it's looking pretty good for us. My hand is down to a single card: the ♣7. The Landlord, to my left, has only four cards left, while my teammate on the right has fourteen. It's my turn, and since I played a bomb (a 6666) last round, I have a free play.\n\nLooking at the game state, it's clear what I need to do. I have a free play, only one card left, and there are no restrictions on what I can play.  My only option is the ♣7, and since it is a legal move, that's what I will play.  This move immediately empties my hand and secures the win for the peasant team.  No need for complex calculations or strategic bluffs here. This is a straightforward, immediate victory.\n\n\n", 'output': 'Evaluation: I have only one card left, the 7 of Clubs. Since I won the previous trick with a bomb and everyone passed, I have a free play. Playing my last card will result in an immediate victory for the peasant team.\n\nReason: This is the winning move. I play my last card to empty my hand and win the game.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♣7"]}'}
